.TH INFINITIME-BUILDER-CLI 1 "" "InfiniTime Builder" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
infinitime-builder-cli \- build customised InfiniTime firmware from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B infinitime-builder-cli
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The command line interface of
.BR infinitime-builder (1).
Without \fB\-\-profile\fR, commands use the selection and sources saved by the graphical
interface.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Show the selected apps and watch faces, in launcher order, and the other available ones.
.TP
.B build
Build a firmware update (DFU zip) and, if needed, a resource pack. Refuses selections that are
clearly too big for the watch's flash unless \fB\-\-force\fR is given.
.TP
.B sizes
Estimate how much flash each app and watch face takes. Runs a one-off measurement build if needed.
.TP
.B validate \fR[\fIpath\fR]
Check a package's \fIinfinitime-app.json\fR (default: the current directory). For app authors.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " file"
Use a profile exported from the graphical interface (\fBlist\fR, \fBbuild\fR, \fBsizes\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-ref " ref"
InfiniTime branch or tag to build.
.TP
.BI \-\-add " source"
Extra package source: \fIowner/repo\fR, a GitHub URL, \fIgithub:owner/repo\fR or a folder.
May be given more than once.
.TP
.B \-\-force
(\fBbuild\fR) Build even if the estimate says the firmware will not fit.
.TP
.BI \-o " dir\fR, " \-\-output " dir"
(\fBbuild\fR) Output directory.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
(\fBbuild\fR) Show the full compiler output.
.TP
.B \-\-remeasure
(\fBsizes\fR) Ignore the cached measurement.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on errors, 130 when interrupted.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
See
.BR infinitime-builder (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
infinitime-builder-cli build \-\-profile my-infinitime.json \-o ~/fw
infinitime-builder-cli validate ~/src/my-watchface
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR infinitime-builder (1)
